-- An @export whose helper REFUSES for one input row and answers for another.
-- The refusing row gets status "refused" (not "error"), and the batch does NOT
-- stop on it: the row after it is still processed.

§ `Export reaching a refusal for some inputs`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`this schedule is not encoded for years before 2000` MEANS
    REFUSE "this schedule is not encoded for years before 2000"

@export f the fee for a rule year
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
f y MEANS
    IF y AT LEAST 2000
    THEN 100
    ELSE `this schedule is not encoded for years before 2000`
